@*
    The Command Stream page shows live device data, lets the user send
    manual override commands and shows suggested actions. The page layout
    uses Bootstrap's 12-column grid (row and col classes), cards and buttons
    (Bootstrap, 2026e; Bootstrap, 2026d; Bootstrap, 2026c). The four counters
    at the top open Bootstrap modals, which are pop-up windows that show the
    detail behind each number, and every suggestion has a "Why?" button that
    opens one too (Bootstrap, 2026f). The table is empty when the
    page loads, and JavaScript fills it with data from the API every two
    seconds using fetch (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026h).
*@

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Command Stream & History";
}

<style>
    .cs-tile {
        cursor: pointer;
    }

        .cs-tile:hover {
            border-color: #4dabf7 !important;
        }
</style>

@* cs-root wraps the whole page, so the click handler below can listen in one place. *@
<div id="cs-root">

    @* Title row with a badge showing whether the page is connected to the API. *@
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-3">
        <h1 class="h3 m-0">Real-Time Command Stream</h1>
        <div>
            <span id="live-indicator" class="badge bg-secondary">connecting...</span>
            <small id="updated" class="text-secondary ms-2"></small>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Four counters that come from the queues in the API: standard queue
       (Queue), priority queue (PriorityQueue), processed readings and the
       duplicate alerts blocked by the HashSet (Nakov and Kolev et al., 2013;
       The IIE, 2026). Each one is a button. data-bs-toggle="modal" and
       data-bs-target make Bootstrap open the modal with that id when the
       button is clicked, without any extra JavaScript (Bootstrap, 2026f). *@
    <div class="row g-3 mb-3 text-center">
        <div class="col">
            <button type="button" class="card cs-tile bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-2 w-100" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#modal-standard">
                <span class="fs-4" id="stat-standard">0</span>
                <small>Standard queue</small>
                <small class="text-secondary">Click for details</small>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <button type="button" class="card cs-tile bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-2 w-100" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#modal-priority">
                <span class="fs-4" id="stat-alert">0</span>
                <small>Priority queue</small>
                <small class="text-secondary">Click for details</small>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <button type="button" class="card cs-tile bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-2 w-100" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#modal-processed">
                <span class="fs-4" id="stat-processed">0</span>
                <small>Processed</small>
                <small class="text-secondary">Click for details</small>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
            <button type="button" class="card cs-tile bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-2 w-100" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#modal-dupes">
                <span class="fs-4" id="stat-dupes">0</span>
                <small>Duplicates blocked</small>
                <small class="text-secondary">Click for details</small>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3">

        @* Left side: search, filters, device table and timeline. *@
        <div class="col-lg-8">

            @* The search box and filters let the user find devices by name,
               category or active alerts (Bootstrap, 2026e). *@
            <div class="row g-2 mb-3">
                <div class="col-md-5">
                    <input id="search" type="text" class="form-control form-control-sm bg-dark text-light border-secondary"
                           placeholder="Search devices..." />
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <select id="category" class="form-select form-select-sm bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                        <option value="">All categories</option>
                        <option value="Environmental">Environmental</option>
                        <option value="PowerConsumption">Power consumption</option>
                        <option value="Actuator">Actuator</option>
                    </select>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3 d-flex align-items-center">
                    <input id="alerts-only" class="form-check-input me-2" type="checkbox" />
                    <label for="alerts-only" class="small">Alerts only</label>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* The table body is empty here. JavaScript adds one row per device. *@
            <table class="table table-dark table-sm table-hover align-middle">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Device</th><th>Category</th><th>Value</th><th>Status</th><th>Control</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="device-rows"></tbody>
            </table>

            @* The timeline graph is drawn here from the sorted history. *@
            <div class="card bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-3">
                <div class="small text-secondary mb-1" id="timeline-title">Timeline (click a device)</div>
                <div id="timeline"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* Right side: suggestions and manual commands. The active alerts
           and the processing log moved into the pop-up windows. *@
        <div class="col-lg-4">

            @* Suggested Actions: predictions from the pattern engine. A
               "habit" suggestion also shows a small table of the latest
               readings of the devices the user keeps searching for. *@
            <div class="card bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-3 mb-3">
                <h2 class="h6">Suggested Actions / Automated Insights</h2>
                <ul class="list-unstyled small mb-0" id="suggestions"><li class="text-secondary">No suggestions yet.</li></ul>
            </div>

            @* Manual override: the ON/OFF buttons send a command, and Undo
               reverses the newest one (the Stack in the API). Bootstrap
               buttons are used for the controls (Bootstrap, 2026c). *@
            <div class="card bg-dark text-light border-secondary p-3">
                <h2 class="h6">Manual override</h2>
                <div class="d-flex gap-2 mb-2">
                    <select id="cmd-device" class="form-select form-select-sm bg-dark text-light border-secondary"></select>
                    <button id="cmd-on" class="btn btn-sm btn-success">ON</button>
                    <button id="cmd-off" class="btn btn-sm btn-danger">OFF</button>
                </div>
                <button id="undo" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-warning mb-2" disabled>Undo last command</button>
                <ul class="list-unstyled small mb-0" id="command-history"><li class="text-secondary">No commands yet.</li></ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ---------- Pop-up windows (Bootstrap modals) ----------
       Each modal has a header with a Close button and a scrollable body
       (modal-dialog-scrollable), so long lists scroll inside the pop-up
       instead of the page (Bootstrap, 2026f). The empty containers are
       filled by JavaScript every time new data arrives, so an open pop-up
       stays up to date. *@

    @* Standard queue: normal readings, first in first out. *@
    <div class="modal fade" id="modal-standard" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="modal-standard-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                <div class="modal-header border-secondary">
                    <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="modal-standard-title">Standard queue (normal readings)</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="small text-secondary">
                        First in, first out: the reading at the top is processed first. The worker
                        empties the queues every half a second, so the waiting list is usually
                        empty; recently processed readings are shown below it. Severity is Critical
                        for an alert, Warning when the value is more than 20% away from the device's
                        recent average, and Normal otherwise.
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="h6" id="standard-waiting-title">Waiting now (0)</h3>
                    <div id="standard-waiting" class="mb-3"></div>
                    <h3 class="h6">Recently processed (newest first)</h3>
                    <div id="standard-recent"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Priority queue: critical alerts, most urgent first. *@
    <div class="modal fade" id="modal-priority" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="modal-priority-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                <div class="modal-header border-secondary">
                    <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="modal-priority-title">Priority queue (critical alerts)</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="small text-secondary">
                        The most urgent alert is served first, whatever order they arrived in.
                        Priority 0 (a power spike) is served before priority 1 (high temperature
                        or low moisture). The worker always empties this queue before the
                        standard queue, so critical alerts skip the line.
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="h6" id="priority-waiting-title">Waiting now (0)</h3>
                    <div id="priority-waiting" class="mb-3"></div>
                    <h3 class="h6">Recently processed alerts (newest first)</h3>
                    <div id="priority-recent"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Processed: every reading handled by the worker (replaces the old processing log). *@
    <div class="modal fade" id="modal-processed" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="modal-processed-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                <div class="modal-header border-secondary">
                    <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="modal-processed-title">Processed readings</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="small text-secondary">
                        Every reading is handled by a background worker. The Queue column shows
                        whether it came from the priority queue or the standard queue. Deviation is
                        how far the value was from the average of that device's last 10 readings.
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="h6">Recently processed (newest first)</h3>
                    <div id="processed-recent"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Duplicates blocked: the HashSet of unique active alerts (replaces the old active alerts card). *@
    <div class="modal fade" id="modal-dupes" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="modal-dupes-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                <div class="modal-header border-secondary">
                    <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="modal-dupes-title">Duplicates blocked</h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="small text-secondary">
                        A set only keeps each item once. While an alert is still active, the same
                        alert arriving again is blocked instead of being processed twice.
                        <strong id="dupes-total">0</strong> duplicates have been blocked so far.
                    </p>
                    <h3 class="h6" id="dupes-active-title">Active alerts (0)</h3>
                    <div id="dupes-active" class="mb-3"></div>
                    <h3 class="h6">Duplicates blocked per alert</h3>
                    <div id="dupes-blocked"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Suggestion details: why one suggested action was made. The text is
       filled in by showSuggestion() when its "Why?" button is clicked
       (Bootstrap, 2026f). *@
    <div class="modal fade" id="modal-why" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="modal-why-title" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable">
            <div class="modal-content bg-dark text-light border-secondary">
                <div class="modal-header border-secondary">
                    <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="modal-why-title"><span id="why-title">Suggestion</span></h2>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <p class="small text-secondary">
                        A Pattern suggestion is learned: the engine counts which events usually
                        follow each other, and its confidence is how often that follow-up really
                        happened. An Insight suggestion comes from a fixed rule, such as a device
                        that stopped sending data or a value outside its normal range. A Habit
                        suggestion appears when the same search is used three or more times.
                    </p>
                    <dl class="row small mb-3">
                        <dt class="col-sm-3">Kind</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-9" id="why-kind"></dd>
                        <dt class="col-sm-3">Confidence</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-9" id="why-confidence"></dd>
                        <dt class="col-sm-3">Device</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-9" id="why-device"></dd>
                        <dt class="col-sm-3">Why it was suggested</dt>
                        <dd class="col-sm-9" id="why-reason"></dd>
                    </dl>
                    <h3 class="h6" id="why-readings-title">Recent readings from this device (newest first)</h3>
                    <div id="why-readings"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script>

        // The page remembers the user's filters, selected device and chosen
        // command device in sessionStorage, so they are still there after
        // navigating to another page and back (Mozilla Developer Network,
        // 2026o).
        var filters = loadFilters();
        var selectedDevice = filters.selectedDevice;
        var actuators = [];
        var lastSuggestions = [];
        var lastData = null;       // the newest snapshot, used by the Why? pop-up

        // Reads the saved filters. Object.assign fills in default values for
        // anything that was not saved, and try/catch protects the page if the
        // saved text is damaged (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026o).
        function loadFilters() {
            try {
                return Object.assign({ search: '', category: '', alertsOnly: false, selectedDevice: '', cmdDevice: '' },
                    JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('cs-filters') || '{}'));
            } catch (e) {
                return { search: '', category: '', alertsOnly: false, selectedDevice: '', cmdDevice: '' };
            }
        }

        // Saves the filters as JSON text. sessionStorage only stores text
        // (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026o).
        function saveFilters() {
            sessionStorage.setItem('cs-filters', JSON.stringify(filters));
        }

        // Makes text safe to place inside HTML. Setting textContent treats the
        // value as plain text, so reading innerHTML afterwards returns it with
        // special characters escaped.
        function esc(text) {
            var div = document.createElement('div');
            div.textContent = text === null || text === undefined ? '' : text;
            return div.innerHTML;
        }

        // Asks the server for the latest snapshot and redraws the page. fetch
        // only fails on network errors, not on HTTP errors like 500, so
        // response.ok is checked as well (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026h).
        // If anything fails, the badge changes to "reconnecting".
        async function poll() {
            if (!document.getElementById('cs-root')) return;

            try {
                var query = new URLSearchParams({
                    search: filters.search,
                    category: filters.category,
                    alertsOnly: filters.alertsOnly
                });

                var response = await fetch('/CommandStream/Snapshot?' + query.toString());
                if (!response.ok) throw new Error('bad response');

                var data = await response.json();
                if (!document.getElementById('cs-root')) return;
                render(data);

                document.getElementById('live-indicator').className = 'badge bg-success';
                document.getElementById('live-indicator').textContent = 'live';

                if (selectedDevice) loadTimeline();
            }
            catch (err) {
                var indicator = document.getElementById('live-indicator');
                if (!indicator) return;
                indicator.className = 'badge bg-danger';
                indicator.textContent = 'reconnecting...';
            }
        }

        // ---------- pop-up helpers ----------

        // Coloured label for a severity: Critical is red, Warning is yellow
        // and Normal is green.
        function sevBadge(severity) {
            var cls = severity === 'Critical' ? 'bg-danger'
                    : severity === 'Warning' ? 'bg-warning text-dark'
                    : 'bg-success';
            return '<span class="badge ' + cls + '">' + esc(severity) + '</span>';
        }

        // Shows a reading's value with its unit. Actuators report "bool", so
        // 1 and 0 are shown as ON and OFF instead.
        function valueText(r) {
            if (r.unit === 'bool') return r.value > 0.5 ? 'ON' : 'OFF';
            return Number(r.value).toFixed(1) + (r.unit ? ' ' + esc(r.unit) : '');
        }

        // Table of readings that are still waiting in a queue. The priority
        // queue also shows the alert name and its priority number.
        function waitingTable(list, withPriority) {
            if (!list || !list.length) return '<p class="text-secondary small mb-0">Empty right now.</p>';

            var head = '<th>#</th><th>Device</th><th class="text-end">Value</th>'
                     + (withPriority ? '<th>Alert</th><th>Priority</th>' : '');

            var rows = list.map(function (r, i) {
                return '<tr><td>' + (i + 1) + '</td><td>' + esc(r.deviceId) + '</td>'
                     + '<td class="text-end">' + valueText(r) + '</td>'
                     + (withPriority ? '<td>' + esc(r.alertType) + '</td><td>' + r.priority + '</td>' : '')
                     + '</tr>';
            }).join('');

            return '<table class="table table-dark table-sm align-middle mb-0"><thead><tr>' + head
                 + '</tr></thead><tbody>' + rows + '</tbody></table>';
        }

        // Table of processed readings, newest first. The mode decides which
        // extra columns are shown: 'priority' adds the alert and priority,
        // and 'all' adds which queue the reading came from.
        function recentTable(list, mode) {
            if (!list || !list.length) return '<p class="text-secondary small mb-0">Nothing processed yet.</p>';

            var head = '<th>#</th><th>Device</th><th class="text-end">Value</th>';
            if (mode === 'priority') head += '<th>Alert</th><th>Priority</th>';
            if (mode === 'all') head += '<th>Queue</th>';
            head += '<th>Severity</th><th class="text-end">Deviation</th><th>Processed</th>';

            var rows = list.map(function (r, i) {
                var extra = '';
                if (mode === 'priority') extra = '<td>' + esc(r.alertType) + '</td><td>' + r.priority + '</td>';
                if (mode === 'all') extra = '<td>' + esc(r.source) + '</td>';

                return '<tr><td>' + (i + 1) + '</td><td>' + esc(r.deviceId) + '</td>'
                     + '<td class="text-end">' + valueText(r) + '</td>' + extra
                     + '<td>' + sevBadge(r.severity) + '</td>'
                     + '<td class="text-end">' + Number(r.deviation).toFixed(1) + '%</td>'
                     + '<td>' + new Date(r.processedAt).toLocaleTimeString() + '</td></tr>';
            }).join('');

            return '<table class="table table-dark table-sm align-middle mb-0"><thead><tr>' + head
                 + '</tr></thead><tbody>' + rows + '</tbody></table>';
        }

        // Table of the latest readings listed inside a "habit" suggestion.
        // The API fills this list with up to six devices that match the term
        // the user keeps searching for, so the user sees the answer without
        // searching again. Bug that was fixed here: the API always sent
        // these readings, but the page never drew them, so the suggestion
        // said "Here are the latest readings below:" with nothing below it.
        // The table is wrapped in Bootstrap's table-responsive so it scrolls
        // sideways inside the narrow side panel instead of breaking the
        // layout (Bootstrap, 2026g). valueText() is reused so actuators show
        // ON and OFF, and esc() keeps every value safe to place in HTML.
        function suggestionReadingsTable(list) {
            if (!list || !list.length) return '';

            var rows = list.map(function (r) {
                var status = r.isOnline
                    ? '<span class="badge bg-success">ONLINE</span>'
                    : '<span class="badge bg-secondary">OFFLINE</span>';

                return '<tr><td>' + esc(r.deviceId) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + esc(r.metric) + '</td>'
                     + '<td class="text-end">' + valueText(r) + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + status + '</td>'
                     + '<td>' + new Date(r.lastSeen).toLocaleTimeString() + '</td></tr>';
            }).join('');

            return '<div class="table-responsive mt-2">'
                 + '<table class="table table-dark table-sm align-middle mb-0"><thead><tr>'
                 + '<th>Device</th><th>Metric</th><th class="text-end">Value</th><th>Status</th><th>Seen</th>'
                 + '</tr></thead><tbody>' + rows + '</tbody></table></div>';
        }

        // Fills in and opens the pop-up for one suggestion. It uses the data
        // from the last refresh, so the pop-up shows the moment it was
        // opened. textContent is used for the text because it never treats
        // the text as HTML. For a suggestion about one device, the readings
        // are that device's entries among the newest processed readings the
        // API sent. A "habit" suggestion has no single device, but it carries
        // its own list of readings, so that list is shown instead. Any other
        // suggestion with no device is about a pattern across the system, so
        // it has no readings. bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(...).show()
        // opens the modal from JavaScript (Bootstrap, 2026f).
        function showSuggestion(index) {
            var s = lastSuggestions[index];
            if (!s || !lastData) return;

            document.getElementById('why-title').textContent = s.title;
            document.getElementById('why-kind').textContent = s.kind;
            document.getElementById('why-confidence').textContent = Math.round(s.confidence * 100) + '%';
            document.getElementById('why-reason').textContent = s.reason;

            var box = document.getElementById('why-readings');
            var boxTitle = document.getElementById('why-readings-title');

            if (!s.deviceId && s.readings && s.readings.length) {
                // Habit suggestion: show the devices that match the search term.
                document.getElementById('why-device').textContent = 'Devices matching "' + s.term + '"';
                boxTitle.textContent = 'Latest readings of the matching devices';
                box.innerHTML = suggestionReadingsTable(s.readings);
            } else if (!s.deviceId) {
                document.getElementById('why-device').textContent = 'No single device';
                boxTitle.textContent = 'Recent readings from this device (newest first)';
                box.innerHTML = '<p class="text-secondary small mb-0">This suggestion is about a pattern across the system, not one device.</p>';
            } else {
                var device = lastData.devices.find(function (d) { return d.deviceId === s.deviceId; });
                document.getElementById('why-device').textContent =
                    s.deviceId + (device ? ' (now ' + valueText(device) + ')' : '');

                boxTitle.textContent = 'Recent readings from this device (newest first)';
                var list = lastData.recentAll.filter(function (r) { return r.deviceId === s.deviceId; });
                box.innerHTML = recentTable(list, 'all');
            }

            bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(document.getElementById('modal-why')).show();
        }

        // Fills in all four pop-ups from the latest snapshot. This runs on
        // every refresh, so a pop-up that is open keeps updating.
        function renderModals(data) {

            // Standard queue.
            document.getElementById('standard-waiting-title').textContent = 'Waiting now (' + data.standardQueued + ')';
            document.getElementById('standard-waiting').innerHTML = waitingTable(data.standardWaiting, false);
            document.getElementById('standard-recent').innerHTML = recentTable(data.recentStandard, 'standard');

            // Priority queue.
            document.getElementById('priority-waiting-title').textContent = 'Waiting now (' + data.alertQueued + ')';
            document.getElementById('priority-waiting').innerHTML = waitingTable(data.alertWaiting, true);
            document.getElementById('priority-recent').innerHTML = recentTable(data.recentPriority, 'priority');

            // Processed readings from both queues.
            document.getElementById('processed-recent').innerHTML = recentTable(data.recentAll, 'all');

            // Duplicates blocked: the unique active alerts (the HashSet), and
            // how many repeats were blocked for each alert.
            document.getElementById('dupes-total').textContent = data.duplicatesBlocked;
            document.getElementById('dupes-active-title').textContent = 'Active alerts (' + data.activeAlerts.length + ')';
            document.getElementById('dupes-active').innerHTML = data.activeAlerts.length
                ? data.activeAlerts.map(function (a) {
                    return '<span class="badge bg-danger me-1 mb-1">' + esc(a) + '</span>';
                }).join('')
                : '<p class="text-secondary small mb-0">No active alerts.</p>';

            document.getElementById('dupes-blocked').innerHTML = data.blockedAlerts.length
                ? '<table class="table table-dark table-sm align-middle mb-0"><thead><tr><th>Alert</th><th class="text-end">Blocked</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
                  + data.blockedAlerts.map(function (b) {
                      return '<tr><td>' + esc(b.alert) + '</td><td class="text-end">' + b.blocked + '</td></tr>';
                  }).join('') + '</tbody></table>'
                : '<p class="text-secondary small mb-0">No duplicates blocked yet.</p>';
        }

        // Draws every part of the page from the data the API returned. The
        // data uses camelCase names (for example deviceId) because that is how
        // ASP.NET Core writes JSON.
        function render(data) {

            // Queue counters.
            document.getElementById('stat-standard').textContent = data.standardQueued;
            document.getElementById('stat-alert').textContent = data.alertQueued;
            document.getElementById('stat-processed').textContent = data.processedCount;
            document.getElementById('stat-dupes').textContent = data.duplicatesBlocked;
            document.getElementById('updated').textContent = 'Updated ' + new Date(data.serverTime).toLocaleTimeString();

            // One table row per device. Actuators get ON/OFF buttons and show
            // their commanded state if a manual command is active; every
            // other device shows its latest value.
            var rows = '';
            data.devices.forEach(function (d) {
                var status = !d.isOnline ? '<span class="badge bg-secondary">OFFLINE</span>'
                           : d.hasAlert ? '<span class="badge bg-danger">ALERT</span>'
                           : '<span class="badge bg-success">OK</span>';

                var value;
                var control = '';
                if (d.category === 'Actuator') {
                    var on = (d.commandedState !== null && d.commandedState !== undefined) ? d.commandedState : d.value > 0.5;
                    value = on ? 'ON' : 'OFF';
                    control = '<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success me-1" data-cmd="on" data-id="' + esc(d.deviceId) + '">ON</button>'
                            + '<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" data-cmd="off" data-id="' + esc(d.deviceId) + '">OFF</button>';
                    if (actuators.indexOf(d.deviceId) === -1) actuators.push(d.deviceId);
                } else {
                    value = d.value.toFixed(1) + ' ' + esc(d.unit);
                }

                rows += '<tr data-device="' + esc(d.deviceId) + '" style="cursor:pointer">'
                      + '<td>' + esc(d.deviceId) + '</td><td>' + esc(d.category) + '</td>'
                      + '<td>' + value + '</td><td>' + status + '</td><td>' + control + '</td></tr>';
            });
            document.getElementById('device-rows').innerHTML =
                rows || '<tr><td colspan="5" class="text-secondary">No devices match.</td></tr>';

            // The command dropdown is only rebuilt when a new actuator
            // appears, so the user's choice is not reset every two seconds.
            var select = document.getElementById('cmd-device');
            if (select.options.length !== actuators.length) {
                var current = select.value || filters.cmdDevice;
                select.innerHTML = actuators.map(function (id) {
                    return '<option value="' + esc(id) + '">' + esc(id) + '</option>';
                }).join('');
                if (current) select.value = current;
            }

            // Suggested Actions. Only suggestions that include a command
            // (a device and ON/OFF) get a "Run" button. A "habit" suggestion
            // (actionType "filter") gets a button with the label the API
            // sent, which fills the search box with its term. Every
            // suggestion gets a "Why?" button that opens a pop-up with the
            // details. A suggestion that carries readings (the habit
            // suggestion) also shows them in a small table under its reason.
            lastSuggestions = data.suggestions;
            lastData = data;
            document.getElementById('suggestions').innerHTML = data.suggestions.length
                ? data.suggestions.map(function (s, i) {
                    var canRun = s.command !== null && s.command !== undefined && s.deviceId;
                    var button = canRun
                        ? '<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info ms-2" data-sug="' + i + '">Run</button>'
                        : '';
                    var filterButton = (s.actionType === 'filter' && s.term)
                        ? '<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info ms-2" data-filter="' + i + '">' + esc(s.actionLabel || 'Show these devices') + '</button>'
                        : '';
                    var why = '<button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary ms-2" data-why="' + i + '">Why?</button>';
                    return '<li class="mb-2"><span class="badge bg-info text-dark me-1">' + esc(s.kind) + '</span>'
                         + esc(s.title) + ' (' + Math.round(s.confidence * 100) + '%)' + button + filterButton + why
                         + '<div class="text-secondary">' + esc(s.reason) + '</div>'
                         + suggestionReadingsTable(s.readings) + '</li>';
                }).join('')
                : '<li class="text-secondary">No suggestions yet.</li>';

            // Command history. The API sends the Stack newest-first, and the
            // Undo button is disabled when there is nothing to undo.
            document.getElementById('undo').disabled = data.commandHistory.length === 0;
            document.getElementById('command-history').innerHTML = data.commandHistory.length
                ? data.commandHistory.map(function (c) {
                    return '<li>#' + c.id + ' ' + esc(c.deviceId) + ' &rarr; ' + (c.newState ? 'ON' : 'OFF') + '</li>';
                }).join('')
                : '<li class="text-secondary">No commands yet.</li>';

            // The pop-up windows (queues, processed readings, alerts).
            renderModals(data);
        }

        // Draws the timeline graph for the selected device. The API sends the
        // readings already sorted by time, because they come from a
        // SortedDictionary (Nakov and Kolev et al., 2013). The values are
        // scaled to fit a 600 x 120 drawing area, then joined by an SVG
        // polyline, which is a line made of connected points
        // (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026m).
        async function loadTimeline() {
            try {
                var response = await fetch('/CommandStream/History?deviceId=' + encodeURIComponent(selectedDevice));
                if (!response.ok) return;
                var points = await response.json();

                var title = document.getElementById('timeline-title');
                if (!title) return;
                title.textContent = 'Timeline: ' + selectedDevice;

                // At least two points are needed to draw a line.
                if (points.length < 2) {
                    document.getElementById('timeline').innerHTML = '<span class="text-secondary small">Waiting for data...</span>';
                    return;
                }

                // x spreads the points evenly across the width. y scales each
                // value between the lowest and highest reading. The "|| 1"
                // avoids dividing by zero when all values are the same.
                var values = points.map(function (p) { return p.value; });
                var min = Math.min.apply(null, values);
                var max = Math.max.apply(null, values);
                var span = (max - min) || 1;

                var coords = points.map(function (p, i) {
                    var x = (i / (points.length - 1)) * 600;
                    var y = 105 - ((p.value - min) / span) * 90;
                    return x.toFixed(1) + ',' + y.toFixed(1);
                }).join(' ');

                document.getElementById('timeline').innerHTML =
                    '<svg viewBox="0 0 600 120" preserveAspectRatio="none" style="width:100%;height:130px">'
                    + '<polyline fill="none" stroke="#4dabf7" stroke-width="2" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" points="' + coords + '"/></svg>'
                    + '<div class="d-flex justify-content-between small text-secondary">'
                    + '<span>min ' + min.toFixed(1) + '</span><span>latest ' + values[values.length - 1].toFixed(1) + '</span><span>max ' + max.toFixed(1) + '</span></div>';
            } catch (err) { }
        }

        // Sends a manual command with a POST request, then refreshes the page
        // data straight away so the user sees the result (Mozilla Developer
        // Network, 2026h).
        async function sendCommand(deviceId, turnOn) {
            if (!deviceId) return;
            await fetch('/CommandStream/Command?deviceId=' + encodeURIComponent(deviceId) + '&turnOn=' + turnOn, { method: 'POST' });
            poll();
        }

        // Asks the server to undo the newest command, then refreshes.
        async function undoCommand() {
            await fetch('/CommandStream/Undo', { method: 'POST' });
            poll();
        }

        // One click listener on the whole page handles every button. This is
        // called event delegation: the table rows and buttons are recreated
        // every two seconds, so listening on the parent keeps them working.
        // closest() finds the nearest parent that matches a selector, which
        // tells us what was clicked (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026k).
        document.getElementById('cs-root').addEventListener('click', function (e) {

            // ON/OFF button inside a table row.
            var cmd = e.target.closest('[data-cmd]');
            if (cmd) { sendCommand(cmd.dataset.id, cmd.dataset.cmd === 'on'); return; }

            // "Why?" button on a suggestion opens its pop-up.
            var why = e.target.closest('[data-why]');
            if (why) { showSuggestion(Number(why.dataset.why)); return; }

            // "Show these devices" button on a habit suggestion. It puts the
            // suggestion's term into the search box and filters the device
            // table, and the choice is saved (Mozilla Developer Network,
            // 2026o). It does not call logSearch(), so using the shortcut
            // does not count as another search and cannot inflate the habit
            // count.
            var filterBtn = e.target.closest('[data-filter]');
            if (filterBtn) {
                var f = lastSuggestions[Number(filterBtn.dataset.filter)];
                if (f && f.term) {
                    document.getElementById('search').value = f.term;
                    filters.search = f.term;
                    saveFilters();
                    poll();
                }
                return;
            }

            // "Run" button on a suggestion.
            var sug = e.target.closest('[data-sug]');
            if (sug) {
                var s = lastSuggestions[Number(sug.dataset.sug)];
                if (s) sendCommand(s.deviceId, s.command);
                return;
            }

            // Undo and the manual override buttons.
            if (e.target.closest('#undo')) { undoCommand(); return; }
            if (e.target.closest('#cmd-on')) { sendCommand(document.getElementById('cmd-device').value, true); return; }
            if (e.target.closest('#cmd-off')) { sendCommand(document.getElementById('cmd-device').value, false); return; }

            // Clicking a table row selects that device for the timeline, and
            // the choice is saved (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026o).
            var row = e.target.closest('tr[data-device]');
            if (row) {
                selectedDevice = row.dataset.device;
                filters.selectedDevice = selectedDevice;
                saveFilters();
                loadTimeline();
            }
        });

        // Restore the saved search, category and alerts-only choices when the
        // page opens (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026o).
        var searchBox = document.getElementById('search');
        var typingTimer = null;

        searchBox.value = filters.search;
        document.getElementById('category').value = filters.category;
        document.getElementById('alerts-only').checked = filters.alertsOnly;

        // Search is "debounced": it waits 300 ms after the user stops typing
        // before asking the server, so it does not send a request for every
        // key press.
        searchBox.addEventListener('input', function () {
            clearTimeout(typingTimer);
            typingTimer = setTimeout(function () {
                filters.search = searchBox.value.trim();
                saveFilters();
                poll();
            }, 300);
        });

        // ---------- search logging (feeds the "habit" suggestion) ----------
        //
        // Every finished search is sent to the pattern engine in the API,
        // which counts how many times each term was searched. Once a term
        // has been searched three times, the engine shows the "I see you have
        // been searching ..." suggestion with the latest readings.
        //
        // Bug that was fixed here: the search used to be sent only from the
        // "change" event. A text box only fires "change" when its text is
        // different from what it was when the box got focus (Mozilla
        // Developer Network, 2026p). Searching the same term again (pressing
        // Enter with the text unchanged, or returning to a box that already
        // held the saved term) never fired it, so the API never received the
        // third search and the suggestion never appeared.
        //
        // The fix is to also listen for the Enter key, which is a search
        // every time it is pressed, and to keep "change" for the case where
        // the user types a new term and clicks away.

        // lastLogged remembers the term and the time of the newest search
        // that was sent. Pressing Enter and then leaving the box fires two
        // events for one search, so without this the same search would be
        // counted twice.
        var lastLogged = { term: '', time: 0 };

        // Sends the current text of the search box to the API through the
        // client controller. The request is a POST because it changes the
        // data the API holds (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026h).
        function logSearch() {
            var term = searchBox.value.trim();
            if (!term) return;

            // Date.now() gives the current time in milliseconds, so two
            // events for the same term less than a second apart are treated
            // as one search (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026r).
            var now = Date.now();
            if (term === lastLogged.term && now - lastLogged.time < 1000) return;
            lastLogged = { term: term, time: now };

            fetch('/CommandStream/LogSearch?term=' + encodeURIComponent(term), { method: 'POST' });
        }

        // Every Enter press counts as a search, even when the text has not
        // changed. The key property tells us which key was pressed
        // (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026q).
        searchBox.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
            if (e.key === 'Enter') logSearch();
        });

        // Typing a new term and then leaving the box still counts as a
        // search (Mozilla Developer Network, 2026p).
        searchBox.addEventListener('change', logSearch);

        // Changing a filter saves it and refreshes the device list.
        document.getElementById('category').addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            filters.category = e.target.value;
            saveFilters();
            poll();
        });

        document.getElementById('alerts-only').addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            filters.alertsOnly = e.target.checked;
            saveFilters();
            poll();
        });

        document.getElementById('cmd-device').addEventListener('change', function (e) {
            filters.cmdDevice = e.target.value;
            saveFilters();
        });

        // Load the data once straight away, then repeat every 2 seconds.
        poll();
        var pollTimer = setInterval(poll, 2000);

        // Called when the user leaves this page, so the timers stop and the
        // page does not keep polling in the background.
        window.pageCleanup = function () {
            clearInterval(pollTimer);
            clearTimeout(typingTimer);
        };

    </script>
}

